70-81df-b9ce99619ece\n\nThe file gives a twelve-gate AND/OR circuit and checks it on all 128 inputs. It proves that every circuit for the graph needs at least eleven binary gates, even if negations are free. A circuit that also uses a NOT therefore has at least twelve gates.\n\nThe lower bound fixes one input after the first binary gate. Four of the six-vertex lower bounds follow from the four-clique lower bound, and exchanging twin vertices handles a fifth. Two exhaustive, kernel-checked searches cover the vertex-0 and vertex-6 deletions.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-25T13:59:56Z","updated_at":"2026-11-25T14:26:23Z","closed_at":"2026-11-25T14:26:23Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"177613a8820e2932d09e1c17762726b42fa11f53","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rammiDgham:L-meta-10556","ref":"L-meta-10556","repo":{"id":1468796644,"node_id":"R_kgDOV4wO5A","name":"pequalnp-proofs","full_name":"rammiDgham/pequalnp-proofs","owner":{"login":"rammiDgham","id":102535680,"node_id":"U_kgDOBhySAA","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/102535680?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham","html_url":"https://github.com/rammiDgham","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rammiDgham/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":fa